    <unit id="=&gt;q42" name="=&gt;q42">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">84</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Musical note - a notation representing the pitch and duration of a musical sound. In Global Music Theory there are many musical temperaments, or tuning systems, but one of the most well-known (if outmoded) is the twelve-tone equal temperament (*12TET*), in which each octave is separated into twelve equally spaced notes, also referred to as semitones or half steps. The scale comprising of all twelve notes is called a *chromatic* scale.::&lt;end&gt;</source>
        <target state="new" />
      </segment>
    </unit>
    <unit id="=&gt;a43" name="=&gt;a43">
      <mda:metadata>
        <mda:meta type="version">1</mda:meta>
        <mda:meta type="pos_id">86</mda:meta>
      </mda:metadata>
