      <segment state="translated">
        <source>::Musical interval - a difference between two pitches.

These are, represented by the number of semitones they encompass:

0 - perfect unison (same note)
1 - minor second
2 - major second
3 - minor third
4 - major third
5 - perfect fourth
6 - diminished fifth/augmented fourth
7 - perfect fifth
8 - minor sixth
9 - major sixth
10 - minor seventh
11 - major seventh
12 - perfect octave::&lt;end&gt;</source>
